---
description: Shared MARKET-MIND-AI project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the root `AGENTS.md` as the project contract. Load only task-relevant guidance from `.agents/skills/`.

The application is harness-independent: Python/FastAPI, React/Vite, SQLite and Docker Compose run without a Claude/Codex-specific runtime. Keep provider interfaces neutral.

The optional n8n integration must remain opt-in and private. Require authenticated human review and importer authorization. Imported workflows remain inactive; do not add activation or execution paths. Keep credentials in deployment secret management and never commit them.

The project MCP server is configured in `.cursor/mcp.json`. Install `backend/requirements.txt`, restart/reload Cursor, and confirm discovery. It is read-only and exposes project capabilities, a fixed engineering-skill allowlist, and n8n JSON validation only. Do not add file-write, network, workflow import/activation/execution, or brokerage tools.

Inspect code and tests before editing. Run relevant checks and distinguish CI verification from a live deployment or real external integration.
